### `docs/decisions/ADR-XXXX-book-covers.md`

```markdown
# ADR-XXXX: Book cover storage

Status: accepted (2026-10-27)

Decision: covers live in SwiftData as a separate `BookCover` entity (optional to-one from `Book`,
cascade delete, inverse declared on `Book.cover` only). It stores a 270 px JPEG thumbnail inline
and a 1200 px JPEG in `@Attribute(.externalStorage)`. The camera original is never persisted.
Downscaling runs in a `@concurrent` function; thumbnails are decoded with `byPreparingForDisplay()`
and cached in an NSCache (40 MB) keyed by `BookCover.id`, which is new for every photo.

Alternatives: (a) JPEG files in Application Support keyed by Book.id: no schema change, but
orphan files, no transactional consistency, own cache busting. (b) Data attributes on `Book`:
every library @Query would load thumbnail bytes for all books.

Cost of change in a year: moving to files is one migration loop over BookCover; Book rows stay small.
CloudKit sync later would need defaults or optionals on BookCover attributes (a migration).
Every ModelContainer opening this store must list BookCover.
```

